PUBLIC RESPONSE: {{1},{2,3},{4,5}}

The Genji-kō patterns assign each of chapters 2–53 a unique set partition of {1,2,3,4,5} (the five incense sticks), with connectivity shown by horizontal bars in the traditional mon diagrams. Chapter 39 (“Yūgiri”) is the diagram whose bars join only sticks 2 with 3 and sticks 4 with 5, leaving 1 isolated; that is exactly the partition {{1},{2,3},{4,5}} when blocks are written in increasing order of their minimal elements. (The supplied example for chapter 20 matches the same canonical ordering of blocks, confirming the representation.) 

(The assignment follows the classical ordering of the mon, which enumerates the 52 partitions precisely once each across those chapters.)

