1.text:
The chapter-20 datum continues to serve as the sole explicit calibration anchor supplied so far. That single reference point already falsifies any stroke-sequence convention that would reorder the five verticals, because the supplied partition for chapter 20 only matches the diagram when the sticks are read strictly left-to-right by column position. Applying that same left-to-right enumeration to the canonical 52-mon list places chapter 39 unambiguously at the 38th pattern, whose diagram joins precisely 2–3 and 4–5 (stick 1 isolated). Sorted by minimal element this is exactly {{1},{2,3},{4,5}}.

The minority reading therefore rests on an inconsistent numbering rule that has already been ruled out by the only concrete datum we possess; until an independent source reproduces the 38th mon under that alternative rule, the stroke-order objection remains unsupported.

